{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 21,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.645,
            0.05,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Operations with Integers"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.101,
            0.589,
            0.125
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.137,
            0.821,
            0.156
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "• When two integers are multiplied, the product is positive when both"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.156,
            0.421,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": "the multiplier and multiplicand are positive, or when both are negative. The product is negative if one of them is positive and the other is negative."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.309,
            0.42,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": "When two integers are divided, the quotient is positive when both the dividend and divisor are positive, or both are negative. The quotient"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.431,
            0.16,
            0.82,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "| - 9 | - 6 | - 3 | 3 | 3 | 6 | 9 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| - 6 | - 4 | - 2 | 2 | 2 | 4 | 6 |\n| - 3 | - 2 | - 1 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n| - 3 | - 2 | - 1 | × | 1 | 2 | 3 |\n| 3 | 2 | 1 | 1 | - 1 | - 2 | - 3 |\n| 6 | 4 | 2 | 2 | - 2 | - 4 | - 6 |\n| 9 | 6 | 3 | 3 | - 3 | - 6 | - 9 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.424,
            0.789,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": "is negative when one of them is positive and the other is negative."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.443,
            0.821,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": "• Integer multiplication is commutative, i.e., for any two integers a and b,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.442,
            0.463,
            0.556,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "a \\times b = b \\times a.",
          "image_source": "images/page_21_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.481,
            0.821,
            0.518
          ],
          "content": "Integer multiplication is associative, i.e., for any three integers, a, b, and c,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.399,
            0.519,
            0.6,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "\\overline{a} \\times (b \\times c) = (a \\times b) \\times c.",
          "image_source": "images/page_21_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.538,
            0.821,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "Integer multiplication is distributive over addition, i.e., for any three integers, a, b, and c,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.379,
            0.577,
            0.619,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": "a \\times (b + c) = (a \\times b) + (a \\times c).",
          "image_source": "images/page_21_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.313,
            0.643,
            0.397,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.647,
            0.56,
            0.669
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "IT's PUZZLE TIME!"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.441,
            0.682,
            0.547,
            0.701
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Terhüchü"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.732,
            0.835,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "Terhüchü is a game played in Assam and Nagaland. The board has 16 squares and diagonals are marked as shown in the following figure. This is usually roughly scratched on a large piece of stone or just drawn on mud. There are 2 players, and each player has a set of 9 coins placed as shown. The coins in one set look different from those in the other set."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.813,
            0.934,
            0.838,
            0.949
          ],
          "content": "45"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
